# Findings acknowledged by fingerprint, one line each.
#
# A fingerprint is `<commit>:<path>:<rule>:<line>` and pins ONE finding in ONE
# historical commit. It cannot mask the same pattern reappearing in a later
# commit, in another file or on another line, which is what makes it the narrow
# way to acknowledge history. Fix the code and leave the past entry here; never
# relax a rule in a `.gitleaks.toml`, which would silence the pattern everywhere.
#
# The fake Google service-account key written by the Workspace Chat test
# fixture. Its key-id field held a sixteen-character hexadecimal literal, which
# the generic-api-key rule reads as a credential by name and entropy. It
# identified nothing: the fixture's private key is generated at test time and
# the fake token endpoint trusts only that. The fixture now builds a
# zero-entropy id, so the line cannot fire again; this entry covers only the
# commit that already shipped.
